SCOPE / PARITY (web source reproduced verbatim — no narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web SubscribeCard is a pure presentational alert-channel discoverability tile (no query / no hook;
its only external dependency is the router <Link>): a bell header "Get notified about incidents", the
self-hosted explainer line, and a grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 grid of five <ChannelTile> rows linking to
the channel setups. Every literal + structure is reproduced:
  • Header  : SF "bell" + t(subscribe.title, "Get notified about incidents")
  • Caption : t(subscribe.description, "Self-hosted: configure your own channels for status events.")
  • Tiles   (web order, lucide -> SF, web `to` preserved):
      Email        Mail->envelope                          "SMTP-based delivery"      /notifications/channels
      Slack        MessageSquare->message                  "Webhook channel"          /notifications/channels
      Discord      Hash->number                            "Webhook channel"          /notifications/channels
      Webhook      Webhook->point.3.connected.trianglepath.dotted "Custom HTTP endpoint" /notifications/channels
      Browser push Smartphone->iphone                      "Opt-in PWA notifications" /settings/notifications
  • Grid    : LazyVGrid; SubscribeCardLayout.columns(width) -> 1 column compact, 2 across regular (web sm:grid-cols-2 @ 640)

Architecture follows the accepted presentational-nav precedent QuickNav (0129): the surface is NOT a
bare static view — it honours the leaf contract through a P1/S8 state-holder seam so every state renders
and previews/tests drive them:
  • P1/S8  state-holder : SubscribeCardChannelSource protocol; SubscribeCardViewModel(@Observable @MainActor);
                          StaticSubscribeCardChannelSource (production, publishes the static catalog, .live);
                          InMemorySubscribeCardChannelSource (preview/test). No HTTP / no navigation in the view.
  • P1/S9  tokens       : Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSMotion only — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex.
  • P1/S10 i18n         : SubscribeCardViewStrings facade (.string/.text), per-surface "SubscribeCard" table;
                          English fallbacks promoted byte-equal from the web literals (no Swift prose).
  • P1/S11 telemetry    : view.opened surface="SubscribeCard" emitted once on first start.
  • Navigation          : onSelect:(SubscribeChannel)->Void — host resolves the deep link (web <Link to>);
                          SubscribeChannel carries webPath (web `to`) + routePath (canonical native route).
  • States (all render) : loading (skeleton grid) / empty (friendly, never blank) / error (retry) /
                          content (the 5-tile grid); ORTHOGONAL connection axis live/stale/offline ->
                          header freshness chip + one-shot stale auto-refresh; header+caption always shown.
  • A11y                : each tile is a Button w/ VoiceOver label ("<label>. <desc>") + hint ("Opens X");
                          header isHeader trait; Dynamic-Type tokens; reduce-motion-aware press feedback.

